; `@std/lsp`: the editor seam. `stdin` is the served relation; a goal on
; `(lsp.stdin 1)` arms the reader. tiny-serve writes one JSON line per
; signed row, `{"rel":"lsp.buffer","sign":1,"args":[...]}` to add and the
; same line with sign -1 to retract. Every `lsp.buffer` line lands as a
; signed row on `buffer`; lines naming another relation are warned and
; skipped.

(: buffer
   (* (: uri str)
      (: version int)
      (: path str)
      (: bytes int)))

(: stdin
   (* (: on int)))
